  "confirm": {
    "Ask": {
      "title": "Apply “Like Garuda Linux (Dr460nized)”?",
      "text": "The look <b>Like Garuda Linux (Dr460nized)</b> will be applied to your desktop.<br><br>What will change: colours, window frames, Qt application style, GTK theme, icons, cursors, fonts, wallpaper, desktop behaviour.<br><br>Rexon builds these parts itself from what your desktop has, close to the original: desktop behaviour.<br><br>Window effects of this look (wobbly windows, magic lamp, cover switch): Rexon will replace the xfwm4 window manager with Compiz. If Compiz does not start, xfwm4 comes back by itself.<br><br>Compiz is built from the AUR: this takes several minutes, and your system will ask for your password.<br><br>Covered by the other parts: global theme — in Plasma it is one package of the parts listed here; on this desktop Rexon applies them one by one<br><br>Covered by the other parts: desktop shell theme — the Xfce panel is drawn by the GTK theme, and the GTK theme of this look is applied<br><br>Partly: colours — Qt programs pick it up after you log in again<br><br>Partly: Qt application style — Qt programs pick it up after you log in again<br><br>Partly: desktop behaviour — not carried over: maximised windows without title bars — Compiz has no such setting<br><br>Partly: desktop behaviour — instead of the desktop name pop-up, Compiz briefly shows its map of desktops when you switch<br><br>Rexon will install the programs it needs: qt6ct, kvantum, beautyline, ttf-fira-sans, ttf-firacode-nerd. Your system will ask for your password.<br><br>Won't be applied: panel layout — Rexon can&#39;t lay out Xfce panels yet, so your panels stay as they are<br><br>You can put everything back at any time with the “Put Back as It Was” button.",
      "yes_text": "Apply",
      "no_text": "Cancel",
      "choices": [],
      "option": null
    }
  },
